ent-WFMobDesertTarantula = desert tarantula
    .desc = A sand-coloured spider the size of a dog. It sits still on the dunes and strikes hard when you walk past.

ent-WFMobCrateMimic = crate
    .desc = A weathered cargo crate, half buried in the sand. The lid looks a little too eager.

ent-WFMerakBarrelCactus = barrel cactus
    .desc = A fat, round cactus. The flesh under the spines is full of water; cut the top off and drink.

ent-WFCactusWater = cactus water
    .desc = Cloudy, slightly bitter water from a barrel cactus. Safe to drink.

ent-WFMerakAgave = agave
    .desc = A rosette of thick, spiked leaves. The cut leaves leak a sweet sap.

ent-WFAgaveSap = agave sap
    .desc = A cut agave leaf dripping with thick, sweet sap. Fine for a still, if you have one.

ent-WFMerakStingNettle = sting-nettle
    .desc = Pale, hairy stalks that pass for dry grass until you brush them. They sting, and your legs go numb for a moment.

ent-WFMerakDatePalm = date palm
    .desc = A shade palm heavy with dates. You can pick them from the lower fronds.

ent-WFMerakDates = dates
    .desc = Sticky, sweet, wrinkled fruit.

ent-WFMerakTumbleweed = tumbleweed
    .desc = A ball of dry stalks, snagged in the sand. It rustles when the wind picks up.

ent-WFMerakSpittingCactus = spitting cactus
    .desc = A red-spined cactus with a swollen crown. It flicks needles at anything it can see, so stay out of its line.

ent-WFMerakCactusSpine = cactus spine
    .desc = A long, sharp needle.

wf-flora-nettle-lash = {CAPITALIZE(THE($plant))} stings your legs!
